  "id": "COMPOUND:15387 - PROTEIN:6150",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a direct relationship between the compound (1S,13S,16S,18R)-18-methoxy-12,15-dimethyl-5,7-dioxa-12,15-diazapentacyclo[11.7.0.01,16.02,10.04,8]icosa-2,4(8),9,19-tetraen-14-one and the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3, through a series of target interactions involving the Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9. This compound is identified as a target of multiple agents, including 2,4-Bis[(4-hydroxyphenyl)methyl]-5-methoxy-3-[2-(3-methoxyphenyl)ethyl]phenol, (2E,4E)-N-isobutylundeca-2,4-dien-8,10-diynamide, and Michaolide J, all of which are known to interact with the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3. The shared target of these agents and the compound’s involvement in the SDR family suggest a potential mechanism of action involving the compound’s ability to modulate the transporter, possibly through direct interaction or by influencing the activity of the SDR family member 9. The evidence supports a pathway where the compound acts as a modulator of the transporter, likely through a mechanism involving the SDR family member 9, which is a key component in the target interaction network.",
